Day</I>&rdquo; means (i) a day on which the Common Stock is listed or quoted and traded on its Principal Trading Market (other than the
OTC Bulletin Board), or (ii) if the Common Stock is not listed on a Trading Market (other than the OTC Bulletin Board), a day on which
the Common Stock is traded in the over-the-counter market, as reported by the OTC Bulletin Board, or (iii) if the Common Stock is not
quoted on any Trading Market, a day on which the Common Stock is quoted in the over-the-counter market as reported in the &ldquo;pink
sheets&rdquo; by Pink Sheets LLC (or any similar organization or agency succeeding to its functions of reporting prices); <I>provided</I>,
that in the event that the Common Stock is not listed or quoted as set forth in (i), (ii) and (iii) hereof, then Trading Day shall mean
a Business Day.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 1in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

